<section class="content">

<h3>3. For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions. The only wrong answer is the one that isn't true.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What has been the happiest moment of your life so far? What made it so special?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Look beneath the surface. Did that moment connect to love, to God, to giving or receiving something that truly mattered?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. In what &laquo;worldly&raquo; things have you placed your hope for happiness &mdash; and have they ever disappointed you?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Money, recognition, romantic relationships, academic success, popularity, appearance, health, comfort... Have any of these let you down? Have any of them delivered less than they promised?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Which beatitude do you find hardest to live? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Examine your heart honestly. Is it poverty of spirit (because you like being in control)? Meekness (because you want to fight back)? Mercy (because someone hurt you deeply)? Purity of heart (because your heart feels scattered)?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Is there someone in your life who seems to live the beatitudes? What impresses you about them?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be a family member, a friend, a teacher, someone at church. What do they have that you want? What makes them different?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. Blessed Chiara Badano was a normal teenager who became a saint through cancer at seventeen. Does her story make holiness seem more possible to you &mdash; or less? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Does Chiara Luce's radical joy in suffering inspire you, intimidate you, or both? What do you think was the &laquo;secret&raquo; behind her happiness?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">6. Which beatitude do you commit to living this week? How will you do it concretely?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Be specific. Not &laquo;I'll be more merciful&raquo; but &laquo;I'll forgive X for Y and not bring it up again.&raquo; Not &laquo;I'll be a peacemaker&raquo; but &laquo;I'll apologize to my sibling for that fight.&raquo; Write the action down.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
