<section class="content">

<h3>4. Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Write Your Own Beatitude</h4>
<p>Imagine Jesus looking at you right now, today, in your exact situation. He knows your struggles, your strengths, your fears. He opens his mouth and says: <strong>&laquo;Blessed are you...&raquo;</strong> What would he say? Write your personal beatitude. Make it real. Make it yours.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. One Beatitude Per Day</h4>
<p>This week, each day choose a different beatitude. When you wake up, read the beatitude of the day (you can use the list below). Ask yourself: <em>&laquo;How can I live this today?&raquo;</em> At the end of the day, write one sentence about how you lived it &mdash; or how you failed to, and what you learned.</p>

<p><strong>Day 1:</strong> Poor in spirit &mdash; practice gratitude; recognize everything as gift.<br />
<strong>Day 2:</strong> Those who mourn &mdash; let yourself feel something deeply today; don't numb out.<br />
<strong>Day 3:</strong> The meek &mdash; don't retaliate when someone annoys you; trust God with the justice.<br />
<strong>Day 4:</strong> Hunger for righteousness &mdash; notice one injustice and do something, however small.<br />
<strong>Day 5:</strong> The merciful &mdash; forgive someone; give something away; serve without being asked.<br />
<strong>Day 6:</strong> Pure in heart &mdash; ask yourself: is my heart divided? What do I want most?<br />
<strong>Day 7:</strong> The peacemaker &mdash; mend a broken relationship or bring calm to a tense situation.<br />
<strong>Day 8:</strong> The persecuted &mdash; stand by a conviction that costs you something small today.</p>

<div style="border:1px solid var(--border);padding:12px;margin:16px 0">
<p><strong>Daily Log:</strong></p>
