<h4>C. The Portrait of Happiness: A Visual Meditation</h4>
<p>Find an image &mdash; a photograph, a painting, a drawing, anything &mdash; that for you represents <strong>true happiness</strong>. It could be a Fra Angelico fresco, a photo of someone you love, or a random image that stirs something in you. Paste it or describe it below. Then ask yourself: <em>Does this image connect to any of the beatitudes? What does it say about what I really want?</em></p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>D. Interview a Living &laquo;Beatitude&raquo;</h4>
<p>Think of someone you know who seems genuinely happy &mdash; not the loud, performative kind but the deep, quiet kind. Approach them and ask (in person, by phone, or by message): <em>&laquo;What is the secret to being as happy as you are?&raquo;</em> Write down their answer.</p>
